.TH demangle 3 "February 2026" "Substrate" "Library Functions"
.SH NAME
demangle \- demangle C++, Rust, and D mangled symbol names
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <demangle.h>
.PP
.BI "char *demangle(const char *" mangled ", int " options ");"
.fi
.SH LIBRARY
libdemangle (\fI-l:libdemangle.a\fR)
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B demangle()
converts a mangled symbol name to a human-readable form.
It supports Itanium C++ ABI symbols, Rust symbols (v0 and legacy), and D symbols.
.PP
If demangling fails, or if the input is not recognized as a supported mangling,
.B demangle()
returns
.BR NULL .
.PP
The caller owns the returned string and must release it with
.BR demangle_free (3).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B DEMANGLE_AUTO
Auto-detect mangling scheme.
.TP
.B DEMANGLE_ITANIUM
Force Itanium C++ demangling.
.TP
.B DEMANGLE_RUST
Force Rust demangling.
.TP
.B DEMANGLE_DLANG
Force D demangling.
.TP
.B DEMANGLE_TYPES
Enable type-only Itanium demangling (for encodings like
.B i
or
.BR PKc ).
.TP
.B DEMANGLE_NO_PARAMS
Suppress parameter lists where supported.
For a D symbol, leave out its type: the name alone,
.BR foo.bar .
.TP
.B DEMANGLE_NO_VERBOSE
Suppress verbose qualifiers where supported.
For a C++ symbol, print the standard abbreviations short, as
.B std::string
rather than
.BR "std::basic_string<char, std::char_traits<char>, std::allocator<char>>" ,
which is otherwise printed as GNU
.BR c++filt (1)
prints it.
For a D symbol, leave out function attributes such as
.BR pure ,
.B nothrow
and
.BR @safe .
.TP
.B DEMANGLE_NO_RECURSE_LIMIT
Lift the bound on how deeply a name may nest.
Without it a name nested more deeply than the parser allows (256 levels
for Itanium C++, 128 for Rust and D) fails to demangle; with it there is
no bound, so a hostile name can exhaust the stack.
This is the flag GNU tools set for
.BR \-\-no\-recurse\-limit .
.SH RETURN VALUE
On success, returns a newly allocated NUL-terminated string.
On failure, returns
.BR NULL .
.SH THREAD SAFETY
Thread-safe and reentrant.
All parser state is local to each call.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
char *s = demangle("_Z3fooi", DEMANGLE_AUTO);
if (s != NULL) {
    /* s == "foo(int)" */
    demangle_free(s);
}
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR demangle_buf (3),
.BR demangle_free (3),
.BR demangle_version (3)
